  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so there is no evidence to exploit; the priority is establishing a clean, interpretable baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest configuration in the search space: it uses the most standard RNA encoder (PCA), the simplest profile setting, and no image or fusion complexity. This experiment (1) establishes the performance floor for the RNA modality with a well-understood pipeline, (2) provides the reference point against which all subsequent multimodal and image-only experiments will be interpreted, and (3) isolates the contribution of the RNA signal before layering in additional design choices. Without this baseline, a multimodal result (e.g., config_016) would be ambiguous—we could not tell whether good performance comes from RNA, image, or their interaction. Under a limited budget, spending the first experiment on the most minimal, confound-free baseline maximizes the interpretive value of every subsequent experiment."
}

